  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I can't figure out what's causing it, but I have not been able to create an impostor of my avatars for a while now: \n\n(avtr_3460b0a5-b357-4fe5-a670-59c08f135083) &\n\n(avtr_aec76abc-33ec-4513-8c5e-6dd37c5ed4b4).\n\nThey have started to fail impostorization after the open beta update where VRCHeadChop was introduced (1431). Before that though, I was able to create an impostor of them just fine.\n\nSo far I have tried:\n\n- Uploading without VRCImpostorSettings, VRCImpostorEnvironment and VRCHeadChop components.\n\n- Uploading to a different Avatar ID.\n\n- Removing all custom Animators, Params and Menu.\n\n- Removing all particle systems.\n\n- Making sure the mesh is humanoid.\n\n- Creating a new project without any custom packages. \n\nBefore it used to say \"An unknown error occurred\", but now it says \"Failed to create Avatar Impostor Prefab\".",
